 	public static void eventExpired(Event cancelledEvent, Set<Meeting> cancelledMeetings) throws Exception {

        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the default behavior of the iCalendar export functionality, which was set to use UTC dates instead of the local timezone. This issue was introduced in a previous commit (592152d), leading to incorrect date representations, especially during daylight savings time changes.

        Commit message:
        iCalendar Exports

- ensure that the exported dates are in the local timezone
- this fixes the issue with daylight savings that was introduced in commit 592152d
  (Biweekly 0.4.3 defaults to UTC dates)  

        Patch:
        diff --git a/JavaSource/org/unitime/timetable/events/EventEmail.java b/JavaSource/org/unitime/timetable/events/EventEmail.java
index f434dcecc..fb40c2f1e 100644
